abstract: >
  Reproducibility bundle for the paper "Reduction of the Wagstaff Chebyshev
  sufficiency conjecture to the Pell Primitive Pair Conjecture" by Alexey
  Dolotov. For W_p = (2^p + 1)/3 and omega_3 = 3 + 2*sqrt(2), the congruence
  omega_3^{(W_p+1)/2} = -1 (mod W_p) (Condition II) holds for every prime W_p;
  whether it implies primality is the open Wagstaff Chebyshev sufficiency
  conjecture, equivalently the open "only if" direction of the Vrba-Reix
  Wagstaff primality test. The paper reduces the conjecture to the Pell
  Primitive Pair Conjecture together with a general-d nonexistence-of-
  compatible-triples (NCT) statement and a mild Wieferich-Wagstaff exclusion,
  and proves NCT unconditionally for every odd d <= 200 and at fifteen further
  parity-unblocked values in (200, 400]. This bundle contains the LaTeX source,
  the reproducibility scripts, and static NCT fixed-d certificates (pinned
  Psi_{4d} factorizations, APR-CL certified).
